       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the maximum labeled metformin dose, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release)\n- **1700 mg PO per day, divided** (for example, 850 mg twice daily)\n- **500 to 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is the more typical dosing\n\nIf you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. If you do, I'll enter it with a note that it is an intentional above-maximum dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
